 {"status": "complete", "type": "task", "created_by": "dogfood-tick-2026-09-23", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": null, "capability_tags": ["dogfood", "seccomp"], "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-23T09:40:26-05:00", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": "0fc950a", "files_changed": null, "lines_added": null, "lines_removed": null, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "glm-5.3-flash@zai-glm-default: standalone/terminal-jail probes seccomp-loader readability (unshare <mapped flags> test -r $SECCOMP_LOADER) before promoting the uid-mapped --user launch; on failure it keeps the command alive on the mapping-less launch with a distinct loud warning naming the unreadable path, the non-traversable-home cause, what still holds, and the TERMINAL_JAIL_UID_MAP=0 remedy; injectable seam TERMINAL_JAIL_SECCOMP_READ_PROBE; 2 new tests RED-proved against the e55acba wrapper.", "foreman_note": "Wave TJ-DF-019+TJ-DF-023 (tick #314, budget 4, 2 dispatched). Foreman verification: scope 2 files; bash -n OK; plugin/test_standalone_cli.py 21 passed; full plugin suite 1405 passed/7 skipped on the branch tip AND on the merged tree 2fff412; uvx ruff check . clean; live --user --seccomp sh -c 'grep Seccomp /proc/self/status' -> Seccomp: 2, no new warning; RED proof reproduced by the foreman in an isolated /tmp harness (both new tests FAIL against the e55acba wrapper). Tier2 judge PASS 7d6c6918 (dir .gitreins/history/2026-09-23/3626eee5), tier1 lint/secrets/tests rc=0; it independently confirmed docs/quickstart.md, install.sh and userns.py untouched. HONEST LIMIT: the mapped launch is not creatable on kara-lair (AppArmor unprivileged_userns), so the unreadable-loader branch is covered by the seam plus the real probe code path, not by a live mapped launch.", "id": "TJ-DF-019", "title": "[P2] fresh-machine `--user --seccomp` fails on any 0700-home host: seccomp loader unreadable under the mapped launch (bunker install leg, live repro)", "priority": "P1", "detail": "2026-09-23 dogfood, fresh Debian 13 bunker agent 3c18196b (destroyed), HEAD b0bd621, install 0s. `terminal-jail --user --seccomp <cmd>` — the exact quickstart §3c form — fails: python3: can't open file '~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/seccomp-loader.py': [Errno 13] Permission denied. Root cause chain: on a mapping-capable host --user takes the uid-mapped launch; the mapped payload runs as subordinate uid 231072; the agent home is mode 0700 (bunkerd default) so DAC denies traversal to ~/.local/lib/terminal-jail/ and python3 cannot exec the loader. Same failure via the repo checkout (app/standalone). Bare `--seccomp` (no --user) works on the same box (Seccomp: 2, filter denies mount mount-rc=32, pivot_root, keyctl EPERM). Host-control repro: this fleet control host (home 711) passes --user --seccomp (Seccomp: 2/1). FIX DIRECTION: ship the loader through a world-traversable install path (e.g. ~/.local/share/terminal-jail or a preflight that copies the loader to a traversable tmp dir before the mapped exec), or probe DAC-traversability of the loader path before taking the mapped launch and degrade with the loud warning the wrapper already uses for --user. Docs: quickstart §3c should note the 0700-home failure mode. Install smoke evidence: /tmp/dogfood-tj/bunker-smoke.sh transcript (host-local).", "created_at": "2026-09-23 04:55:00", "worktree": "/home/kara/worktrees/terminal-jail-TJ-DF-019", "branch": "wt/TJ-DF-019", "sessions": ["terminal-jail-2026-09-23-13-46-44"]}
 {"status": "complete", "type": "task", "created_by": "dogfood-tick-2026-09-23", "complexity": 2, "depends_on": null, "blocks": null, "primary_model": null, "primary_provider": null, "fallback_model": null, "fallback_provider": null, "reasoning": null, "capability_tags": ["dogfood", "seccomp"], "worker_status": "complete", "dispatched_at": null, "completed_at": "2026-09-23 12:55:00", "attempts": 0, "exit_code": null, "commit_hash": "156815b", "files_changed": null, "lines_added": 210, "lines_removed": 7, "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "GREEN", "worker_summary": "Added clock_adjtime NR 305 to x86_64 deny list (glibc routes adjtimex() there); repaired BPF fall-through jf skip that silently bypassed 9 deny NRs incl. adjtimex itself (finding premise partly wrong — 159 EPERM was CAP-check coincidental); new TestGlibcVariantNrs libc-wrapper EPERM regression tests. Red-proofed: old filter returned ret=0 for libc adjtimex.", "foreman_note": "Judge PASS verdict e016124e (.gitreins/history/2026-09-23/, task_id-matched) with independent BPF simulation + red-proof. Foreman re-verified: pytest test_seccomp 47 passed/3 skipped, full plugin suite 1403 passed/7 skipped, live ctypes probe adjtimex ret=-1 errno=1 under filter, NR 305 in deny table, ruff format clean on touched files. Whole-tree ruff format lint FAIL = pre-existing TJ-GAP-075 debt, not this change. aarch64 mirroring deferred (TODO in code, needs aarch64 host).", "id": "TJ-DF-020", "title": "[P2] seccomp deny list misses glibc-routed variant syscalls: adjtimex(2) succeeds under the filter via clock_adjtime(305)", "priority": "P2", "detail": "2026-09-23, control host x86_64, HEAD 271c30b. The filter is real and denies 10/11 deny-NR probes with EPERM (pivot_root, mount, acct, settimeofday, swapon, swapoff, create_module, kexec_load, add_key, keyctl, clock_settime — in-process probe /tmp/dogfood-tj/probe-all-nrs.py; request_key returned ENOKEY=126, a harness artifact not a bypass). BUT libc adjtimex() routes to clock_adjtime(NR 305), which is NOT in the deny list, so `python3 -c \"ctypes...adjtimex(0)\"` inside the jail succeeds (ret=0). glibc generally routes classic time/module syscalls to their _time64/variant forms (clock_adjtime, clock_settime64, finit_module aarch64), so the x86_64 classic-NR list may systematically miss the modern entry points. FIX DIRECTION: add the variant NRs (x86_64: clock_adjtime=305, and audit settimeofday→clock_settime family, init_module→finit_module already present, kexec_load→kexec_file_load already present) to _DENY_EXTRA with a comment on glibc routing; add a raw-syscall regression test that calls each libc WRAPPER (not the raw NR) under the filter and asserts EPERM. Evidence: adjtimex ret=0 errno=0 under filter, raw syscall(159,...) EPERM — same process, same filter.", "created_at": "2026-09-23 04:55:00", "updated_at": "2026-09-23 12:55:00"}
